WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.243 --> 00:00:08.080
Speaker 1: And while we're on the subject of&nbsp;
things Trump has done, we obviously have to talk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.760
about all of the investigations against him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:19.200
because recently Michael Cohen, Donald Trump's&nbsp;
former lawyer slash fixer, came out in an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:26.720
interview and suggested that there is going to&nbsp;
be, quote, so much flipping. On Donald Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:34.800
once all of these investigations get to that&nbsp;
point. And of course, the big one recently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:39.120
last week, Allen WEISSELBERG Trump&nbsp;
Organization chief financial officer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:45.440
pleaded guilty to 15 different counts. Every&nbsp;
count, by the way, that he was charged with, he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:51.280
pleaded guilty to. They didn't drop any of them.&nbsp;
So he had to plead to each and every one of them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:56.240
And he's only going to get five months on&nbsp;
Riker's Island. He is eligible for early&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:00.080
release after 100 days. So he's going to&nbsp;
spend a little over three months in there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:05.520
But the judge did warn him last week, if you do&nbsp;
not cooperate fully, truthfully and honestly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:10.080
I can put you away for 10 to&nbsp;
15 years on Rikers, which,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:16.080
given your age, is pretty much a life sentence.&nbsp;
And here's the best part about Weisselberg's.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:27.280
Cooperation. With the prosecutors. He can't plead&nbsp;
the Fifth. He cannot plead the Fifth Amendment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:34.480
because he's already pleaded guilty to all of&nbsp;
the crimes he was accused of. A plea of guilty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:40.320
basically does away with your Fifth Amendment&nbsp;
rights of self-incrimination because you've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:46.720
already admitted you did the things kind of like&nbsp;
the acceptance of a presidential pardon. If you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:52.160
accept a presidential pardon. Our Supreme Court&nbsp;
says you can no longer plead the Fifth because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.160 --> 00:02:00.960
acceptance of a pardon is an acceptance of guilt.&nbsp;
So Weisselberg literally has no choice. All right.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:06.480
You either go to Riker's Island for 15 years,&nbsp;
which probably would be the rest of his life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:14.080
Or you give us every single thing on Donald Trump.&nbsp;
You can't get out of it. You can't excuse it. You&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:21.840
can't, you know, call in sick. You can't plead the&nbsp;
Fifth. You can do nothing to stop what's coming.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:26.400
And of course, that was just one of the examples,&nbsp;
of course, that Michael Cohen recently gave.&nbsp;&nbsp;

